ioned sometimes hundreds kilometers  from the border russia russia has long  and big borders why particularly the  border near ukraine  but uh did what what is different from  what was happening before because there  were maneuvering of russian troops on  the border with ukraine on the border  with other countries on other parts of  our territory before 100 000 that many  that's that's quite a big amount that's  what's concerning the west is this is  this is being excused as military  operations it's a very extensive  military operation happening close we  can we can argue how many miles from the  ukrainian border but it's the closest it  can get to the ukrainian border  well these are only claims first of all  and secondly i quoted to you the  ukrainian minister of defense which i do  not you do not usually do but still he  says that there is no significant  deployment at the border which with  which would uh signif which would mean  that uh russia is preparing an attack  so that's how i saw the headlines today  uh this morning in the news even  ukrainians are now doubtful about these  facts so i think only united kingdom and  united states maybe are promoting this  uh these uh allegations and this version  of the events again nothing  extraordinary is happening we are moving  troops in our border in our territory uh  we have all the rights to do so we have  done this before there can be different  explanations to this and these all  explanations it is our national matter  there can be maneuvering of the troops  there can be  the uh  i don't know exercises of the troops  that are being conducted and this is not  linked to some imminent or not imminent  military operation every country does  this i know that there are nato  maneuvering not far from our borders and  nobody is uh seems to be preoccupied by  this in the west though it's uh exactly  provocative okay so  why so much about this this information  i can't really understand it happens in  the heads of our of our western  colleagues and no nowhere else so you so  you feel that the west is making a big  deal out of this if that is the case why  why is russia entering into weeks worth  of talks with nato allies about the  what's happening on the border  but it's not about what's happening on  the border this perception is absolutely  absolutely wrong this is western  perception we are entering the talks  about  security guarantees which are not  related at all with the situation on the  board with ukraine so that's not how we  see the situation  but western leaders are looking at these  talks and it is being pegged as to  what's happening on that border and  they're looking for reassurances that  ukraine is secure and nato allies are  helping ukraine as a defensive measure  it's not about reassurance for western  countries and for ukraine it's about  reassurances for russia and we started  these negotiations it was our initiative  we proposed the draft treaties with the  united states and with nato it's not  about the situation on the border with  ukraine or whatever it's about long-term  ironclad  legal guarantees for russia which are  long overdue and uh if you look at the  texts of what we proposed  uh this is about this and the  interpretation that it's about  de-escalating of situation the border is  totally the invention of our western  colleagues talk to me about then what it  is you talk about russia wants  reassurances what reassurances does  russia want what does russia want from  these talks then because what the west  is seeing is russia uh coming  looking for looking for something and  they're seeing all the troops masked on  the border with ukraine and seeing it as  uh a non-verbal threat if you like  uh russia wants reassurances about our  security our security has suffered a lot  because of nato enlargements because of  the  promises that were were made by the west  that were not kept after that at  perestroika time and in the 90s and  it's it's it's diffi